RF.put("questb:b18",{"8658":{"id":8658,"t":"Striker's Leggings","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Skin of the Great Sandworm, 2 Idols of the Sun, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nSkin of the Great Sandworm Ouro\n2 Idol of the Sun Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"You seek to prove your worth to my kind, mortal? Very well, perhaps we can be of mutual assistance.\nThe ancient sandworm, Ouro, is a being of legendary power. He is rumored to have been created by the Old God himself as a mockery of life.\nHis skin is unnatural... thick, nearly impregnable, yet it's flexible and allows him to move with the speed and grace of a much smaller creature.\nBring me a sample of his skin along with other minor components and I shall craft you leggings of great power.","rew":"You will receive:\nStriker's Leggings\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Hunter Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8658\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Striker's Leggings this quest\nBring the Skin of the Great Sandworm, 2 Idols of the Sun, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"98418":{"id":98418,"t":"Shared fury","lv":30,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 5 Xavian Rogues, 5 Felsworn, 5 Betrayers, and 5 Hellcallers.\nReturn to Maseara Autumnmoon in Forest Song afterwards.\nXavian Betrayer slain : 0/ 5\nXavian Felsworn slain : 0/ 5\nXavian Hellcaller slain : 0/ 5\nXavian Rogue slain : 0/ 5","desc":"Kurothel mentioned sightings of what they say are wolf-men. Those of the pack now lurking in greater numbers in our forest. Last we had spoken, druids were pursuing communication with those of the beast heart who displayed measured control of their animal instincts.\nHis written words show a darker struggle. If there is anything we can do to help see HIM again, surely quelling the demon threat that is driving him to this burning transformation will be of aid to his anguished soul.\nSlay the Xavian, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":81,"y":50.2,"n":"Maseara Autumnmoon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"738":{"id":738,"t":"Find Agmond","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Agmond.","desc":"Prospector Agmond was in charge of our excavation sites in the Badlands, to the southwest. I say \"was\" because...well, I haven't heard from him in weeks. I need you to find Agmond so I can get his report.\nLast I heard Agmond was at the southernmost dig site in the Badlands--a tiny operation past the Angor Fortress. I'd start your search for him there.","rew":"You will receive:\nRipped Prospector Belt Jade 2 Gold Ore\nMoney: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,450\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","done":"This skeleton must be the unfortunate remains of Agmond. His body is broken and battered, and his bones picked clean.\nLoch Modan Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":65.9,"y":65.6,"n":"Prospector Ironband","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":50.9,"y":62.4,"n":"Battered Dwarven Skeleton","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"2258":{"id":2258,"t":"Badlands Reagent Run","lv":39,"min":36,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Buzzard Gizzards, 10 Crag Coyote Fangs, and 5 Rock Elemental Shards to Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath, Badlands.\n5 Buzzard Gizzard Giant Buzzard 20 % , Starving Buzzard 15 % , Buzzard 5 %\n10 Crag Coyote Fang Feral Crag Coyote 80 % , Rabid Crag Coyote 80 % , Elder Crag Coyote 80 % , Crag Coyote 80 %\n5 Rock Elemental Shard Lesser Rock Elemental 20 % , Greater Rock Elemental 20 % , Enraged Rock Elemental 20 % , Rock Elemental 15 % and 4 more","desc":"‹name›, I could use your aid if you're up for it. I am an alchemist of some note, and I seek your aid in acquiring some reagents found out in the Badlands.\nI need the following items to replenish my stocks: five buzzard gizzards, ten crag coyote fangs, and five rock elemental shards. Obviously, you can get them off of the beasties themselves; if you're not the fighting type, then find friends who are.\nAcquire these items for me, you'll get some coin out of the deal. Watcha wanna do?","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,000\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Have you gotten the things I need yet? You won't get paid unless you bring me those reagents.","done":"Ah, well done! These should last me for a little while, at least. Here is your pay as promised.\nIf you're interested, I have some more reagents I could use. These, however, are only found in the depths of the Uldaman excavation. They will not be easy to get, but I will make it worth your while if you are interested in helping me again.\nPerhaps something more than some shiny coins, yes?","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.4,"y":46.1,"n":"Jarkal Mossmeld","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"1618":{"id":1618,"t":"Gearing Redridge","lv":16,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Tormus Deepforge wants you to bring 4 Runed Copper Belts and 4 Heavy Copper Mauls to Verner Osgood in Redridge.\n4 Runed Copper Belt\n4 Heavy Copper Maul","desc":"We dwarves aren't the only ones fighting. Our human allies have their hands full too!\nRedridge is under periodic attack from blackrock orcs, and their supply of equipment is always low. If you were to help them out, I'm sure their resident blacksmith, Verner Osgood, would teach you a trick or two.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Ironforge Breastplate\nExperience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I hope you're here with good news from Ironforge. Because I'm at my wit's end!","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. This will help me out tremendously. With the Blackrock orcs attacking from Stonewatch Keep and the Redridge gnolls lurking in the foothills to the north, I'm always fixing armor and making new weapons for our troops.\nThe supplies you brought will give me a moment's peace. I will have enough time to teach you something...\nDun Morogh Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.9,"y":27.9,"n":"Tormus Deepforge","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":25.9,"y":47.3,"n":"Verner Osgood","e":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97938":{"id":97938,"t":"Camping 101 alchemy","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Cyndra Kindwhisper in Dolanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your alchemy skill to 20","desc":"So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Mana Well. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":60.6,"n":"Cyndra Kindwhisper","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96658":{"id":96658,"t":"Camping 101 cooking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with William Pickman in Brill to learn to become a cook.\nLearn cooking from William Pickman in Brill","desc":"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, ‹class›. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","back":"A good campfire is the foundation to any good camp.","done":"With this, you'll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you've learned is just the basics, so you won't be able to place too many furnishings around it.\nRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.\nYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you're savvy in their skills.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.8,"y":51.4,"n":"William Pickman","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"2178":{"id":2178,"t":"Easy Strider Living","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring back 5 Strider Meat to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine.\n5 Strider Meat Strider Clutchmother 56 % , Foreststrider 44.7 % , Foreststrider Fledgling 42.6 % , Greater Plainstrider 41.5 % and 3 more","desc":"Do you smell that delicious aroma? It's my secret recipe, ‹name›--fresh strider stew. Delicious!\nPerhaps you would be interested in learning the recipe?\nBefore I teach you the recipe, you will need to prove that you can handle the beasts.\nNow, I don't expect you to go out and tame one and ride it back to me, but if you can kill a few and bring back some of their succulent meat, I may be persuaded to show you the ways of strider stew.","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Strider Stew 5 Strider Stew\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The pot is empty and I'm hungry! What's taking you so long?","done":"Fantastic! Try it and tell me what you think, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.7,"y":40.7,"n":"Alanndarian Nightsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["cooking"]},"94338":{"id":94338,"t":"Craftsmans writ goblin jumper cables xl","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Goblin Jumper Cables XL\nGoblin Jumper Cables XL","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Goblin Jumper Cables XL, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Goblin Jumper Cables XL Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94338","cats":["crafting"]},"94258":{"id":94258,"t":"Craftsmans writ lesser stoneshield potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Lesser Stoneshield Potion\nLesser Stoneshield Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Lesser Stoneshield Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nSilithus Orgrimmar Darnassus\nSilithus Open the zone on the world map Start an item: Craftsman's Writ: Lesser Stoneshield Potion Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94258","cats":["crafting"]},"7938":{"id":7938,"t":"Your Fortune Awaits You...","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Deadmines in Westfall and seek out your fortune.\nSayge's Fortune #24\nProvided: Sayge's Fortune #24","desc":"\"Your fortune awaits you inside the Deadmines.\"\nThe fortune Sayge handed you feels slightly warm to the touch. Grasping it firmly, you see an image of the Deadmines inside Westfall's ruined hamlet of Moonbrook. Focusing closer in on the image, you wind about twisty passages until you reach a shimmering portal... one that leads into the heart of the mines itself. Stepping through it, a strange chest appears out from nowhere.","rew":"You will receive:\nMysterious Lockbox\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"This chest looks like the one from your vision...","done":"A quick search of the chest reveals a lockbox from within it! It would seem that you have found your fortune!\nStart an item: Sayge's Fortune #24 End Mysterious Deadmines Chest The Deadmines Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Shareable No Quest ID 7938","cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"1138":{"id":1138,"t":"Fruit of the Sea","lv":17,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 6 Fine Crab Chunks for Gubber Blump in Auberdine.\n6 Fine Crab Chunks Encrusted Tide Crawler 40 % , Reef Crawler 40 %","desc":"I love crab. Crabs are the fruit of the sea! You can bake it, barbecue it, boil it, and broil it. They're pan fried, deep fried, and stir fried. There's crab salad, crab soup, crab stew, pepper crab, lemon crab, whipper root crab, and Ironforge surprise crab. That's... that's about it.\nI'm here fishing right now, so I can't get any fine crab chunks. You can pick them out of reef crawlers and encrusted tide crawlers. You can make a lot with it. You can bake it, barbecue it, boil it...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nShucking Gloves Crustacean Boots\nExperience: 1,250\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"...lemon crab, whipper root crab, and Ironforge surprise crab. That's about it.\nOh, hello there ‹name›. Do you have them fine crab chunks I was telling you about?","done":"Wow, these fine crab chunks are what I need. Thanks ‹name›! I found this while I was fishing a while ago, and I have no use for it. Maybe you can do something with it. It sure don't make any good crab dishes.\nI told you all about crabs, right?","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.1,"y":44.9,"n":"Gubber Blump","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"2098":{"id":2098,"t":"Gyromast's Retrieval","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and return the three pieces of Gelkak's Key to Gelkak Gyromast.\nTop of Gelkak's Key Giant Foreststrider 20 %\nMiddle of Gelkak's Key Greymist Tidehunter 10 % , Greymist Oracle 10 % , Murkdeep 1 % , Greymist Hunter 1 % and 4 more\nBottom of Gelkak's Key Raging Reef Crawler 20 % , Encrusted Tide Crawler 5 %","desc":"A pirate's life ain't an easy one, landlubber. It ain't all about plunderin' and booze! Alas, me ship be sunk just off shore thanks to them pesky Threshadons.\nWhat I be needin' is me first mate back in workin' order!\nWhen I washed up'n shore, the key for me first mate broke on the rocks and was pilfered by the beasties of Darkshore. Out of the corner of me eyes I saw some of them Ragin' Crawlers, Ferocious Foreststrider, and murloc rummaging through the wreckage....","rew":"Money: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Have ye found me broke down key, landlubber?","done":"Avast ye scurvy sea dog! Ye did it! Soon me first mate be back in workin' order and them beasties won't know what hit em!\nHrm, have ye seen me first mate?","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":56.7,"y":13.5,"n":"Gelkak Gyromast","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1458":{"id":1458,"t":"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc.","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Hatefury Claws, and 10 Hatefury Horns to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.\n10 Hatefury Claw Hatefury Hellcaller 30 % , Hatefury Shadowstalker 30 % , Hatefury Betrayer 30 % , Hatefury Felsworn 30 % and 3 more\n10 Hatefury Horn Hatefury Hellcaller 30 % , Hatefury Shadowstalker 30 % , Hatefury Betrayer 30 % , Hatefury Felsworn 30 % and 3 more","desc":"One of my tasks out here involves picking up some reagents for Leftwitch, a gnome mage in Kharanos . Roetten seems to think it's easy coin in the bank since we're out here already. He doesn't really care that we're short-handed as is.\nThe first few items on his list should be easy enough to get, and it'd be a good chunk of coin for anyone helping me out.\nI need some horns and claws from the Hatefury satyr to the east of here. Bring 'em back to me and we'll get started on the rest of the list.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Despicable creatures, the satyr. Story says they're somehow tied to the night elves, but I'm not so sure I believe it.\nI think they get that on account of that one elf that brought them into the war few years back. World's never been the same since. Lot more dangerous, and a lot scarier.","done":"Good good, ‹name›. Not sure if these are of any good quality, but if Leftwitch wanted a specific type, he should have specified before sending the Reclaimers out here to begin with.\nWhat say you to getting on with the next item on his list?","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.2,"y":9.6,"n":"Kreldig Ungor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"92818":{"id":92818,"t":"Big no massive iron axes","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 2 Massive Iron Axes to Grolkar in the Magram Village in Desolace.\n2 Massive Iron Axe\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"WE NEED MORE WEAPONS.\nMORE. WEAPONS.\nHOW ELSE IS THE MAGRAM GOING TO SMASH PUNY GELKIS?\nI WANT TO SEE WHAT YOU CAN MAKE, OUTSIDER. BRING ME AXES. BIG, NO, MASSIVE ONES.\nHURRY UP.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPlans: Hard Gold Gauntlet Plans: Iron Morningstar\nMoney: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,050\n+1,000 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 92818","cats":["desolace"]},"98738":{"id":98738,"t":"Blessings of the great windborne cat spirit","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","desc":"Now that you have received my blessing, return to Dendrite. He will instruct you further.\nUnfortunately I have little left to teach you for the moment. I do hope you come and visit me in Zephras again someday. I sense promise in you, young shen'dorei.\nMay the shadows forever hide you, your foes easily fall prey to your claws, and the winds guide your steps.","done":"<Dendrite makes another invisible gesture in the air above him as you approach. Another aura of power comes over him, and he smiles ever so slightly.>\nI sense the cunning and ferocity of the cat within you that was not present when I sent you to meet the Great Cat Spirit. In your eyes I can sense you now understand the stealth and speed needed to adopt this nature.\nNow you may learn to focus your cunning and adopt the true nature of the cat and call upon its spirit.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":43.9,"y":73.4,"n":"Avatar of Saeyleenan","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"818":{"id":818,"t":"A Solvent Spirit","lv":7,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Intact Makrura Eyes and 8 vials of Crawler Mucus to Master Vornal in Sen'jin Village.\n4 Intact Makrura Eye Slimeshell Makrura 65 % , Makrura Elder 65 % , Makrura Snapclaw 65 % , Makrura Shellhide 65 % and 1 more\n8 Crawler Mucus Surf Crawler 50 % , Encrusted Surf Crawler 50 % , Corrupted Surf Crawler 50 % , Pygmy Surf Crawler 50 %","desc":"Although my eyes fail me, I still can see clearly enough. More often I must rely on my alchemical skills to aid me in magics that once came easily. But I refuse to take on an apprentice--no troll or orc worthy enough has ever come forward.\nAre you worthy? Yes, of course you are... of course you think you are.\nI need a few things. Will you get them for me?\nI need intact makrura eyes, and vials of crawler mucus. You can find them on any makrura or crawler in Durotar. We shall speak again soon.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Really Sticky Glue\nMoney: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Time is the true test of your strength and will. Lose patience or give in to weakness, and your true self will be shown.","done":"Well done, young one... well done indeed.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":55.9,"y":74.4,"n":"Master Vornal","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"98":{"id":98,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":35,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Ring of Ruin.","obj":"Kill Stalvan Mistmantle and show Madame Eva his family ring.\nMistmantle Family Ring Stalvan Mistmantle","desc":"Stalvan Mistmantle led a life of depravity. Innocent victims died by his hand. Undoubtedly he is guilty of countless crimes. Now the lunatic threatens Darkshire. The Light only knows what sordid acts he is plotting. Travel to his cottage just north of town, ‹class›, and execute Stalvan, once and for all.\nWhen the deed is done, travel to Madame Eva's and show her his family ring. After all, it was her premonition that led to this gruesome discovery. But Darkshire is safer because of her.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCrescent of Forlorn Spirits Ring of Forlorn Spirits Ring of Ruin\nNew in Forever: Ring of Ruin.\nExperience: 4,100\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes, ‹name›?","done":"I know, ‹name›: Stalvan is dead. I sensed a wave of hope ripple through the tainted forest. Once and for all, Duskwood is free from his blood thirst. My joy is hampered by thoughts of those who fell prey to the horrible beast. Nonetheless, you are a brave and cunning ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.5,"y":46.8,"n":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":45.3,"n":"Madame Eva","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1218":{"id":1218,"t":"Soothing Spices","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Soothing Spices to \"Swamp Eye\" Jarl in Dustwallow Marsh.\n3 Soothing Spices sold by Gunder Thornbush , sold by Banalash , sold by Nerrist , sold by Edna Mullby and 4 more","desc":"I like cooking. Good swamp cooking. Fried green frog legs and the like.\nAnd for cooking, I need spice. Soothing spice. Then I'll make a stew and stew it up and suck it down and give you some too.\nDo you like stew?","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Frog Leg Stew\nExperience: 1,350","back":"Spice. We could all use some spice in our life. You agree?","done":"Ah, that's the spice! Now here's some swampy good stew.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":55.4,"y":26.3,"n":"\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"18":{"id":18,"t":"Brotherhood of Thieves","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 Red Burlap Bandanas to Deputy Willem outside the Northshire Abbey.\n12 Red Burlap Bandana Defias Thug 80 %","desc":"Recently, a new group of thieves has been hanging around Northshire. They call themselves the Defias Brotherhood, and have been seen across the river to the east.\nI don't know what they're up to, but I'm sure it's not good! Bring me the bandanas they wear, and I'll reward you with a weapon.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMilitia Dagger Militia Hammer Militia Shortsword Militia Warhammer Militia Quarterstaff\nExperience: 360\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you gathered those bandanas for me yet?","done":"Back with some bandanas, I see. The Stormwind Army appreciates your help.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.2,"y":42.9,"n":"Deputy Willem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"2978":{"id":2978,"t":"The Gordunni Scroll","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Gordunni Scroll to Rok Orhan in Camp Mojache.\nGordunni Scroll Gordunni Scroll\nProvided: Gordunni Scroll","desc":"Picking up the soiled scroll, you notice that it seems to be depicting some sort of meeting or ceremony. Rok Orhan would be interested in this scroll, and what it might mean to the Gordunni.","rew":"Experience: 1,800\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"What is this?","done":"This scroll... You found this in the Gordunni Outpost?","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.5,"y":27.9,"n":"Gordunni Scroll","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":75.8,"y":43.6,"n":"Rok Orhan","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"498":{"id":498,"t":"The Rescue","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Krusk in Tarren Mill needs you to free Drull and Tog'thar from Durnholde Keep.\nRescue Drull\nRescue Tog'thar","desc":"Me and some other warriors were sent by the Warchief to retrieve an object from Durnholde and to investigate this so-called Syndicate.\nWe went to Durnholde to take a look around, but we were taken by surprise by a large number of the humans. We fought bravely, but their sheer numbers were enough to defeat us. They took a few of us captive, but I was able to escape.\nDurnholde is just southeast of here, across the river. Drull and Tog'thar are being held there, you must go and rescue them.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGrunt Vest Orcish War Chain\nYou will also receive:\nRecipe: Big Bear Steak\nExperience: 2,200\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You must make haste, ‹class›. I shudder to think what the humans might be doing to Drull and Tog'thar.","done":"So the humans thought to turn our warriors into slaves, did they? We'll show them!\nIt would seem that they have taken Gol'dir, our leader, to another location. We must find him and rescue him. But we currently have no clue where he is...\nWhen we have a lead, I will be sure to tell you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":63.2,"y":20.7,"n":"Krusk","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"658":{"id":658,"t":"Hints of a New Plague?","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Forsaken Courier and bring back her Sealed Folder to Quae near the Go'Shek Farm.\nSealed Folder Forsaken Courier","desc":"So, Phin sent you to check on us? Not surprised--he worries too much.\nWe've been watching the farm for days, and Kin claims she saw a courier come out of that small house to the south not long ago.\nShe talks a lot, but I can always trust her senses when we're in dangerous areas.\nYou wouldn't happen to be a skilled tracker, would you? We think the courier might be carrying notes to Tarren Mill. If we could get our hands on those documents, it might shed some light on what's happening in Hillsbrad.","rew":"Experience: 2,800\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"We appreciate your help in looking for that courier, ‹name›.\nWhile you were gone, Kin saw an apothecary come out of that same house to the south of here. I'm confident that they're up to no good--I just need proof of it before we go off and do something rash.\nHave you had any luck yet?","done":"Excellent!\nLet's see what this is about...","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":60.2,"y":53.8,"n":"Quae","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"94978":{"id":94978,"t":"Taming the beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Windsong Crawler found near bodies of water.\nPractice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.\nTame a Windsong Crawler\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"Every hunter begins by learning the bond between beast and master. This is your first challenge. In time, you'll tame creatures from every corner of the world, but for now, start with our rivers and lakes on Zephras.\nTake this Taming Rod and seek out a Windsong Crawler.\nShow that you can earn its trust, and begin your path toward true mastery.","back":"You will learn, Venator, and one day you will be a great ‹class›.","done":"Well tamed, Venator! You are becoming adept already.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59.6,"y":72.6,"n":"Quel'ana Quickgale","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"418":{"id":418,"t":"Thelsamar Blood Sausages","lv":11,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 pieces of Bear Meat, 3 Boar Intestines, and 3 Spider Ichor to Vidra Hearthstove in Thelsamar.\n3 Boar Intestines Battle Boar Horror 51.5 % in Razorfen Downs , Withered Battle Boar 51.3 % in Razorfen Downs , Raging Agam'ar 49.2 % in Razorfen Kraul , Agam'ar 48.8 % in Razorfen Kraul and 4 more\n3 Bear Meat Giant Ashenvale Bear 71.4 % , Elder Ashenvale Bear 55.6 % , Thistle Bear 46.9 % , Giant Grizzled Bear 45 % and 4 more\n3 Spider Ichor Naraxis 53.2 % , Wildthorn Lurker 51.2 % , Black Widow Hatchling 47.3 % , Deepmoss Creeper 47.3 % and 4 more","desc":"There's never a shortage of empty bellies here in Thelsamar, kids running in and out, workers from the excavation coming in after a hard day's work. We're famous for our blood sausages, I don't suppose you've ever tried them?\nNo? Well, around here you've got to work for your meals, and don't think just because you're a fancy ‹class›, you'll be any exception.\nI'll need bear meat, boar intestines for the casings, and spider ichor for spice. You get me some of those, and leave the cooking to Vidra!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Blood Sausage Recipe: Blood Sausage\nMoney: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 875\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I'm all ready to start cooking, do you have the ingredients for me?","done":"Trust me, it seems a lot harder than it looks, but...\nOh, I've never known someone to take much interest in the making of sausages, but I'll give you the recipe just in case. Here you go, mind you eat them fresh!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":34.8,"y":49.3,"n":"Vidra Hearthstove","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"258":{"id":258,"t":"A Hunter's Challenge","lv":17,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 5 Elder Mountain Boars and return to Daryl the Youngling in the Farstrider Lodge within 12 minutes.\nElder Mountain Boar slain : 0/ 5","desc":"‹name›ath, is it? I can tell you're bursting with pride over completing the first test, hm? As I told you before, it's no large feat.\nYou should try your hand at boar hunting. Trust me, this is no Coldridge Valley boar hunt, so you'd best have a care with them. I'll give you just twelve minutes this time.\nDon't feel bad if you fail. I'd give you the shirt off my back if you succeeded!\nHave I ever related to you the story of how I received my famous scar? No? It was two years ago...","rew":"You will receive:\nFine Cloth Shirt Daryl's Shortsword\nExperience: 950","back":"It's only natural to feel sorry for yourself when shown up by someone so new to this world. You shouldn't feel bad, ‹name›.\nHm? Did I get your name wrong?","done":"You seem a bit worse for wear. No doubt the boars gave you some trouble, hm? No worries, I will be discreet about your struggle, I can imagine how hard it must be for you without the accusations of wagging tongues.\nOh! You managed to kill the boars? I... well, that is... that is to say, I'm not surprised! Any child could have--bet?\nWhat bet?","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":83.5,"y":65.5,"n":"Daryl the Youngling","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"1938":{"id":1938,"t":"Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic","lv":28,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic to High Sorcerer Andromath in Stormwind.\nUr's Treatise on Shadow Magic Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic","desc":"Long ago, three mages studied in this tower until one fell to the dark arts. He was urged to turn away from that evil magic, but he could not resist. And so he was banished.\nThe fallen mage's new domain is the tower of Ilgalar in Redridge, and he took with him a powerful book--Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic.\nWe, the mages of Stormwind, would have that book returned. Enter the tower of Ilgalar, find the tome in his library, and bring it to me.","rew":"Experience: 2,300","back":"Do you have the book, ‹name›? Its secrets are not meant for the untrained, and plumbing its depths can lead to doom and ruin.","done":"I feared that Morganth had hidden the book elsewhere, or that he had found a way to open it and read its contents.\nIt is good to see that he did not, and that the seals we placed on Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic still hold.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.7,"y":87.6,"n":"High Sorcerer Andromath","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"8578":{"id":8578,"t":"Scrying Goggles? No Problem!","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Narain's Scrying Goggles and return them to Narain Soothfancy in Tanaris.\nNarain's Scrying Goggles Flamewaker 1 % , Flamewaker Protector 1 % , Lava Surger 1 % , Lava Reaver 1 % and 4 more","desc":"<You hear a sigh of relief escape the crate.>\nYou just want his scrying goggles? Great! That will be no problem... Just give me a minute to... Hey! Where the... Dagnabbit!\nWell, there's some bad news and some worse news. The bad news is that I lost the goggles. The worse news is that I lost them when I was nosing around in the Molten Core last month. Yep, the Molten Core... I guess that concludes our business! Bye!","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Major Rejuvenation Potion\nExperience: 8,300\n+10 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"The Molten Core, eh? I hope my goggles are still in one piece!","done":"Outstanding! Now where did I put that 500 pound chicken and Volume II of \"Draconic For Dummies???\" Oh, and here's a little something for all your hard work!\nSilverpine Forest Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":46.2,"y":86.7,"n":"Inconspicuous Crate","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","e":1}],"cats":["molten-core"]},"9058":{"id":9058,"t":"Cryptstalker Boots","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Leopold at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Cryptstalker Boots if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Boots, 12 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 3 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Boots Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Gothik the Harvester 0 % in Naxxramas , Instructor Razuvious 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n3 Nexus Crystal","desc":"I have discovered a use for the carapace of the crypt fiend. I am able to fashion an extremely light and very deadly set of armor by combining the fragments with some of the desecrated magical armors lost in Naxxramas.\nBring me the items I require and I shall fashion for you a suit of armor the likes of which has never before been seen in our world!","rew":"You will receive:\nCryptstalker Boots\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Cryptstalker Boots.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.9,"n":"Huntsman Leopold","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8978":{"id":8978,"t":"Return to Mokvar","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Mokvar in Orgrimmar with the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer.\nExtra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer\nProvided: Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer","desc":"It's been great working with you, ‹name›. Here is the finished product.\nI hope it helps you in your current endeavors. And hey, if you don't mind, help spread the word. I wouldn't mind having more customers!","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"You've returned with the device?","done":"You've returned with the device! I'm impressed by your dedication, ‹name›. Excellent work.\nTanaris Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Mux Manascrambler","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1778":{"id":1778,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.","desc":"I'm going to see about making plans to return home soon. Hopefully, Stephanie is doing well back in Stormwind. I can't wait to see her again. Till next we meet, ‹class›.","rew":"Experience: 230","done":"So, you've returned so quickly, huh? And what pray tell have you accomplished in your time away from here?\nWere you able to help a noble cause? Perhaps you've learned the value of charity or some more about your obligations to the citizens of Azeroth. Tell me, who have you helped and how.... Impressive, ‹name›, those are surely the actions of one who follows the Light.\nSuch sacrifice will always be rewarded in time.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.8,"y":31,"n":"John Turner","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":23,"n":"Tiza Battleforge","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"91858":{"id":91858,"t":"Diplomatic incident","lv":22,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Travel to The Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest and speak with Trevan Rol about the missing Earthen Ring travelers.","desc":"A most unfortunate turn of events in Silverpine has presented a unique opportunity for us to prove our worth in the eyes of the horde.\nA pair of dignitaries from the Earthen Ring went missing in Silverpine Forest en route to Tarren Mill. We don't know much else but rumors say that this is becoming quite the diplomatic incident. If we can recover these missing persons, it could help gain us the legitimacy we so dearly need.\nWe have a man at The Sepulcher, Trevan Rol. Travel there and speak with him.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 440\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"Danitha sent you? Well in that case I already know why you are here. You just walked into a damned fine mess, ‹class›.\nTirisfal Glades Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Danitha Morr","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":41,"n":"Trevan Rol","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"8418":{"id":8418,"t":"Forging the Mightstone","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the voodoo feathers to Ashlam Valorfist.\n2 Amber Voodoo Feather Gasher , Zul'Lor\n2 Blue Voodoo Feather Hukku , Mijan\n2 Green Voodoo Feather Zolo , Loro","desc":"Now we must combine the inert scourgestones and create a weapon to shatter the ranks of undead. This is no trivial task, ‹name›. Only the trolls of the sunken temple carry the kind of rare magic able to turn the evil of something against itself.\nIn the temple, the trolls are known as Gasher, Mijan, Zolo, Hukku, Zul'lor, and Loro. Do not feel remorse for their corrupt souls... they are not without evil.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLightforged Blade Sanctified Orb Chivalrous Signet\nYou will also receive:\nHoly Mightstone\nMoney: 1 55 1 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,350\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Have you slain the wretched trolls?","done":"This is excellent, ‹name›. I would say I am surprised, but I knew without question that you wouldn't let us down.\nIt is my honor to bestow one of the Holy Mightstones to you. Use it well.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"94818":{"id":94818,"t":"Contingency plan","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","done":"Continue your service to the Light and you will become a great ‹class›, ‹name›. Maintain your vigilance and dedication!\nYou are ready for your next lesson in service.","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":24.8,"y":10,"n":"High Priestess Mims","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"178":{"id":178,"t":"Theocritus' Retrieval","lv":23,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Faded Shadowhide Pendant to Theocritus the Mage.\nFaded Shadowhide Pendant\nProvided: Faded Shadowhide Pendant","desc":"<You hear a disembodied voice...>\nDo not be alarmed. I am Theocritus, High Mage of Tower Azora in Elwynn Forest. The pendant you are holding is a method of communication between the Shadowhide Gnolls and their master, Morganth.\nThrough months of research, I believe I too can communicate through these pendants. If you can hear this message, then my spell was a success.\nBring me this pendant and I will reward you for the service.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Restoring Balm\nMoney: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,400\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I spoke to you through a pendant, you say? Hmm...give it to me, so that I might study it.","done":"You have my gratitude, ‹name›. I sent that message to the Shadowhide Pendants weeks ago and had believed it a failure. But it seems the spell did reach at least some pendants, after a significant delay.\nIn time I hope to learn how to send an attack through the pendants, to immobilize any Shadowhide Gnolls who wear them.\nBut before that is possible, I'm afraid that much more research is required.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":65.2,"y":69.7,"n":"Theocritus","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8818":{"id":8818,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Horde Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with the Darkspear tribe.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":33,"y":71.6,"n":"Thunder Bluff Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":46.3,"y":35.1,"n":"Officer Vu'Shalay","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"1858":{"id":1858,"t":"The Shattered Hand","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Steal Tazan's key, then use it to open his Satchel and deliver its contents to Therzok in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.\nTazan's Logbook\nProvided: Tazan's Satchel","desc":"I'll leave it to you to get Tazan's satchel open, and return to me with its contents. The locking mechanism is complex, so it would probably be easiest if you obtained the key.\nAs you didn't find it on Tazan's body, I can only assume that he left the key in the care of another... Ah, yes, that's right. He had an assistant named Gamon. A drunkard, you'll most likely find him at the tavern. Perhaps you could quietly relieve him of the key.","rew":"You will receive:\nBlade of Cunning\nExperience: 460","back":"Is it not vexing to have the subject of your desire within your grasp, but to have no way of getting to it?","done":"Hmmm, now this is interesting. You've more than proved your worth with this, ‹name›. I am quite impressed. Consider yourself the newest member of the Shattered Hand. And take this, it will be a great help to you in the future, I think.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.7,"y":53.6,"n":"Therzok","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"3378":{"id":3378,"t":"Prayer to Elune","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Prayer to Elune and take it to Astarii Starseeker in Darnassus.\nPrayer to Elune Twilight Idolater , Twilight Geomancer , Twilight Dark Shaman , Twilight Fire Guard","desc":"Will you assist me, mortal? Will you find the prayer to Elune?\nAs I stated, the prayer was etched onto a golden tablet. One of these idol worshipping scoundrels must have it on their person.\nIf you do recover my prayer, take it to Astarii Starseeker in Darnassus. It matters little that my faith has been rekindled after the countless malevolent actions that I have taken against this world and its inhabitants, but my prayer must be heard. Absolution is the last thing I expect.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nKaylari Shoulders Runesteel Vambraces\nMoney: 1 45 1 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,900\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"What brings you to the Temple of the Moon, ‹name›?","done":"Elune smiles upon you this eve, ‹name›. You have returned a lost soul to her. Please accept this as a token of our gratitude.\nSearing Gorge Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":29.6,"y":26.3,"n":"Zamael Lunthistle","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.3,"y":81,"n":"Astarii Starseeker","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8898":{"id":8898,"t":"Dearest Colara,","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Creased Letter to Colara Dean outside the bank in Stormwind.\nCreased Letter\nProvided: Creased Letter","desc":"I met a lass in Stormwind when I was last there on the bank's business. She stole my heart away. Now, I can't stop thinking about her! I'd like to send her this message - I've rewritten it twelve times!\nThe mail is so full now, and I want to make sure it gets there.\nIf you're heading that way, could you help me?","back":"Hello there, handsome. Something I can help you with?","done":"Tormek? Oh yes, I do remember him. He had quite a nice beard and smile underneath.\nAh, I can't believe he remembered me!\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.3,"y":31.7,"n":"Tormek Stoneriver","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.7,"y":75.5,"n":"Colara Dean","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8258":{"id":8258,"t":"The Darkreaver Menace","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 14,500, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Use the Divination Scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement in the Scholomance. Doing so will bring forth spirits you must fight. Defeating these spirits will summon forth Death Knight Darkreaver; defeat him.\nBring Darkreaver's Head to Sagorne Creststrider in the Valley of Wisdom, Orgrimmar.\nDarkreaver's Head Death Knight Darkreaver\nProvided: Divination Scryer","desc":"Death Knight Darkreaver lords over the Great Ossuary in the Scholomance. He threatens to twist the spirit realm to do his own bidding, and he must be stopped! This is where the scryer you helped make comes into play.\nUse the divination scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement to call forth Darkreaver's spirit minions. Defeat the spirits and the death knight himself will appear. ‹name›, bring me his head! Only his demise will reverse the damage done to the spirit realm!","rew":"You will receive:\nSkyfury Helm\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Horde","back":"Time is critical, ‹name› - have you succeeded in stopping Death Knight Darkreaver's threat?","done":"This is a victory to savor, ‹name›! The demise of Darkreaver should restore the fragile fetters that anchor the spirit realm.\nYou have far exceeded what was asked of you, even when you had no notion of reward or compensation. You are truly a ‹class› of worth, my friend.\nI know that acting to preserve the spirit realm should be thanks enough, but please - accept this simple gift with my thanks.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.7,"y":35.9,"n":"Sagorne Creststrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"93058":{"id":93058,"t":"Saving our own","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis clan, and rescue 5 Gelkis Captives within the Valley of Bones. Return to Nerlokh near the entrance when you are done.\nGelkis Captive rescued : 0/ 5\nGelkis Clan Centaur","desc":"There was a brief battle between a few of the necromancers just around the hill, and I used that to take a closer look inside.\n‹name›, not all of our recent losses were defectors. There are Gelkis being held captive further in the valley! I was not able to investigate their situation because a hulking Magram brute started charging my direction. I consider myself fortunate he lost interest quickly.\nYou must go back into the Valley of Bones and free them. The Gelkis stand together.\nLevel 42 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 38 40 45 53 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93058\nThe chain\n3 quests from level 42 to 43, 6,360 XP in all.\n1 [ 42 ] Saving Our Own this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis clan, and rescue 5 Gelkis Captives within the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n2 [ 43 ] Checking Things Out\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and investigate centaur points of interest within Shen'dralas.\n360 XP\n3 [ 42 ] Khan Jehn\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and slay Khan Jhen at Magram Village.\n3,450 XP","cats":["shendralas"]},"8738":{"id":8738,"t":"Hive'Regal Scout Report","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Contact Cenarion Scout Landion inside Hive'Regal and return the Hive'Regal Scout Report to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold. You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing VII in order to complete this quest.\nHive'Regal Scout Report\nTactical Task Briefing VII\nProvided: Tactical Task Briefing VII","desc":"We've sent our best scouts deep into the silithid hives to gather intelligence. Scout Landion has been watching the silithid movements at Hive'Regal for several days now. Find him and obtain a written report. We need to be able to act on that information as soon as possible, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Tactical Badge Followup Tactical Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You'll find Scout Landion inside Hive'regal. Hurry, ‹name›! Time is of the essence.","done":"Your efforts are greatly appreciated, ‹name›. I'll read these scouting reports right away, feel free to go over your next assignment.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8498":{"id":8498,"t":"Twilight Battle Orders","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Obtain the Twilight Battle Orders and bring them Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing X in order to complete this quest.\nTwilight Battle Orders Twilight Prophet\nTactical Task Briefing X\nProvided: Tactical Task Briefing X","desc":"Our scouts have reported new battle orders being issued by the Twilight's Hammer leaders. The orders are being distributed by Twilight Prophets under heavy escort. Intercept the orders and bring them to Commander Mar'alith.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Tactical Badge Tactical Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You've brought something for me?","done":"Excellent. It's important to stay ahead of the enemy's next move. This information will allow us to anticipate the Twilight's Hammer's attacks.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"1058":{"id":1058,"t":"Jin'Zil's Forest Magic","lv":26,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Witch Doctor Jin'Zil at Malaka'jin wants 5 portions of Stonetalon Sap, 5 Twilight Whiskers, 30 Courser Eyes and a Fey Dragon Scale.\n5 Stonetalon Sap Sap Beast 80 %\n5 Twilight Whisker Twilight Runner 80 %\n30 Courser Eye Antlered Courser 80 % , Great Courser 80 %\nFey Dragon Scale Fey Dragon 80 % , Wily Fey Dragon 80 % , Nal'taszar 80 %","desc":"So excited I am!\nThree little cages for three little elves! But what shall we do with our lovely tree-hugging friends? Why, let's give them a taste of... what do they call it... forest magic!\nI'll need a good mess of Stonetalon sap. From those horrid felines, bring me some twilight whiskers. This calls for plenty of courser eyes, of course -- can never have enough eyes. Oh, and lest we forget, a precious scale from a fey dragon.\nHurry to Stonetalon Peak, ‹name›, so I can brew some forest magic!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nVoodoo Mantle Hexed Bracers\nExperience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Look at our poor little elf friends. All caged up with no forest to frolic in!\nNow were you able to find me some sap? How about the whiskers from the twilight runners? Don't suppose you have that fey dragon scale on you?\nAnd eyes! I'll need so many eyes! You just can't mix up a fierce forest magic brew without a good helping of eyes!","done":"Oh how happy these little woodland nymphs shall be! We'll make them feel right at home with this special concoction!","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":74.5,"y":97.9,"n":"Witch Doctor Jin'Zil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"97538":{"id":97538,"t":"Pigments for paints","lv":26,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Tah Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff wants 30 Mirkweed Pods from Mirkfallon Lake.\n30 Mirkweed Pods","desc":"Greetings, friend. I wonder if I may ask a favor of you? I have just run out of red pigment for my paints, and I am looking for one with younger hooves to make the long journey into the Stonetalon Mountains on my behalf.\nIn the middle of the mountain pass there lies a large circular lake, Mirkfallon Lake, that has a unique plant that grows within its waters. The pods of this plant, mirkweed, turn a vibrant red when dried. Gather the pods of this plant for me, and I will reward you well for your efforts.","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":54.2,"y":47.4,"n":"Tah Winterhoof","s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"578":{"id":578,"t":"The Stone of the Tides","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the haunted island for Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.\nProvided: Library Scrip","desc":"If there is indeed a goblin mage and water elementals haunting the island, it could mean the Stone of the Tides can be mine!\nI want you to locate this haunted island... find out what's going on. Oh, and if you perhaps want to find out more about the Stone of the Tides, take this scrip to the Stormwind Library, they should be able to find you a copy of the book I first came across the legend in.\nCould it be that Gazban actually discovered the Stone...?","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"The trolls truly possessed some amazing magical objects, ‹name›. And now, perhaps, I have the opportunity to add one to my extensive collection. Did you have any luck finding the source of the rumor?","done":"So the stories were true! Incredible!\nHowever, we will need to figure out a way to defeat the curse of the Stone of the Tides, if we are to retrieve it. The curse is magical business, we'll need one of those wizards to help us out.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":76.9,"n":"Baron Revilgaz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"338":{"id":338,"t":"The Green Hills of Stranglethorn","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect the missing pages from The Green Hills of Stranglethorn manuscript. Once all four chapters are complete, return them to Barnil.\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Chapter I\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Chapter II\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Chapter III\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Chapter IV","desc":"Master Nesingwary will be so upset if he finds out!\nHe trusted me to proofread the manuscript of his novel, The Green Hills of Stranglethorn. Everything was going well, but a large gust of wind blew through the camp and scattered the pages everywhere!\nI was able to gather most of the pages but many are still strewn about the jungle. Collect the pages to complete each of the four chapters.\nI will help you organize them. Return the chapters to me once you have all four.","rew":"You will receive:\nJungle Boots 2 Thick Armor Kit 3 Superior Healing Potion\nExperience: 4,700","back":"Have you assembled the chapters yet, ‹name›?","done":"You've certainly saved me a heap of trouble, ‹name›! I can't thank you enough. It shouldn't be long now until we see Master Nesingwary's book in libraries throughout the world!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.5,"n":"Barnil Stonepot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"2498":{"id":2498,"t":"Return to Denalan","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rellian Greenspyre wants you to speak with Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.","desc":"I have just received word that Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth has discovered what may be the cause of the tumors that plague the timberlings. Please speak with him, and tell him I sent you.\nMake haste, ‹name›; he needs our help.","rew":"Experience: 80\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Ah, so Rellian sent you to aid me. I am glad you arrived here so soon.\nI have discovered something quite disturbing!\nDarnassus Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.2,"y":21.6,"n":"Rellian Greenspyre","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Denalan","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"978":{"id":978,"t":"Moontouched Wildkin","lv":55,"min":52,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 10 Moontouched Feathers from Winterspring, then return to Erelas Ambersky in Rut'theran Village.\n10 Moontouched Feather Moontouched Feather","desc":"Wildkin feathers from the Hinterlands appear to contain traces of magical qualities. These powers... they don't seem to be wielded by the creatures, it's more like they are simply inherent to the species -- part of their very essence.\nDuring my studies, I heard that a large population of wildkin inhabit the snowy lands of Winterspring. Could these creatures have the same powers? Please help me find an answer, ‹name›. Go to Winterspring and gather feathers that have dropped to the ground, then return to me.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Where could these powers have originated from? I think we are on the right track to find the answer, ‹name›.","done":"Now I can compare the feathers... Let's see...\nTeldrassil Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.5,"y":92,"n":"Erelas Ambersky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"898":{"id":898,"t":"Free From the Hold","lv":20,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Embroidered Leggings.","obj":"Safely escort Gilthares Firebough back to Captain Brightsun in Ratchet.","desc":"Finally! Someone to rescue me!\nI can't believe you got past the guards. These zealots from Theramore are out of their minds. They sank our ship and imprisoned me, the only survivor. I was called an enemy and threat to the Alliance.\nMe! A threat to their great sham of an Alliance? I was a deckhand on a moonshine transport between Ratchet and Booty Bay.\nEnough talk. Help me get back to Ratchet will you? Let me know when you're ready and we'll make our break.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBuckled Boots Riveted Gauntlets Embroidered Leggings\nNew in Forever: Embroidered Leggings.\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+150 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Yes?","done":"And to think, we thought Firebough was long dead!\nYour heroics have earned you a place of honor with the Thalo'dan Privateers, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62,"y":55,"n":"Gilthares Firebough","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.3,"y":39,"n":"Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"96898":{"id":96898,"t":"Remnants of war","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 12 Necrotic Crystal Fragments in Tirisfal Glades.\n12 Necrotic Crystal Fragment","desc":"It wasn't long ago that the citadel of Naxxramas bore down upon this city, intent on wiping the Forsaken off the map. Both the Forsaken and the Argent Dawn lost much that day to secure the future of the Forsaken.\nDuring the battle, the great necrotic focusing crystal hanging beneath Naxxramas was shattered and its fragments were scattered all over this area. I suspect that is what the cultists are here for. Help me recover the fragments and deprive the scourge of them.","back":"I'd advise you not come into too much physical contact with those crystals. Even shattered and spent, the lingering magic in these necrotic crystals is highly dangerous.","done":"Thank you. This should slow the efforts of the scourge in this area. I suspect the denizens of Tirisfal will be pulling these crystals out of the ground for years, but removing the most conspicuous of them can only help.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.8,"y":61,"n":"Hadric Harlson","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2418":{"id":2418,"t":"Power Stones","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Charged Leather Bracers. Reported by players.","obj":"Bring 8 Dentrium Power Stones and 8 An'Alleum Power Stones to Rigglefuzz in the Badlands.\n8 Dentrium Power Stone Shadowforge Sharpshooter 40 % , Shadowforge Ambusher 40 % , Shadowforge Geologist 40 % , Shadowforge Archaeologist 40 % and 4 more\n8 An'Alleum Power Stone Shadowforge Sharpshooter 55 % , Shadowforge Ambusher 55 % , Shadowforge Geologist 55 % , Shadowforge Archaeologist 55 % and 4 more","desc":"A while ago, I had an incident with the Shadowforge Dwarves. They brought me to Angor Fortress to study two types of strange stones from Uldaman. I discovered that the stones were sustained, stable power sources if treated correctly. It's amazing the things one can find in that old dig site!\nAnyway, after I told them the secret of the stones they kicked me out of Angor Fortress and began digging for more in Uldaman.\nI want those stones for myself! Bring me both types and I'll pay you plenty!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEnergized Stone Circle Duracin Bracers Everlast Boots Charged Leather Bracers\nNew in Forever: Charged Leather Bracers.\nExperience: 3,500\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Do you have the power stones, ‹name›? I have a robotic rodent that needs a power supply...","done":"That's great, you found some! Thanks a lot, ‹name›. You're the most dependable ‹race› I've met!\nI can't wait to try these on some devices I've been tinkering with. I bet that, under the right circumstances, devices powered with these stones will keep going, and going, and going...\nBadlands Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":42.4,"y":52.9,"n":"Rigglefuzz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"2338":{"id":2338,"t":"Translating the Journal","lv":42,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Let Jarkal borrow the necklace. In exchange, he will translate the journal for you.\nUntranslated Journal\nProvided: Untranslated Journal","desc":"Droffers and Son Salvage aren't smart enough to restore the magic in the necklace, but I am. All I want to do is study the necklace so I can learn to make them myself. To do that, I will need your necklace. Let me borrow it, and in exchange for the time I get to study it I will translate the journal for you. While you are searching for the gems, I should have enough time to learn what I need to.\nIt's a simple deal, and no one else will be the wiser. Whatcha wanna do?","rew":"Experience: 350\n+10 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"You've thought about it, yes? You're a smart ‹class› if you take this deal - you and I will get what we both want, and Droffers and Son Salvage will think they're getting what they want.","done":"You know a good deal when you see one - I knew I could count on you.\nIt will be just a moment while I cast a spell to quickly translate the human tongue into a form you will understand. I am a troll of my word; ask anyone in the Horde about Jarkal Mossmeld. Now, let's get this started...","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.4,"y":46.1,"n":"Jarkal Mossmeld","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"4738":{"id":4738,"t":"In Search of Menara Voidrender","lv":31,"min":31,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.","desc":"Let us be clear about one thing, ‹name›: I don't feel you are ready for such responsibilities. I don't think aiding in the creation of any item of power is something a novice should ever be involved in; especially one so untested.\nBut that's not my decision. The powers that be, or at least the ones that do wish to impart such gifts upon you get to decide that.\nIf you're interested in learning more, I suggest you seek out Menara Voidrender in Ratchet. She usually resides in the tower above the port town.","rew":"Experience: 625","done":"Ah, Demisette sent you. Good. Then word does reach far enough to find future students. This pleases me.\nIt is typical of our kind, ‹name›, to band together, regardless of race. It is especially important since those we deal with most do not discriminate in their malice if we fail to appease them or control them properly.\nI feel you've learned a great many things, and if you are willing, I would help you create tools to compliment your skills.\nStormwind City The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85,"n":"Demisette Cloyce","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1698":{"id":1698,"t":"Yorus Barleybrew","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Yorus Barleybrew.","desc":"Yorus Barleybrew has issued a challenge to all able warriors of the Alliance. He waits at the Lakeshire Inn, in Redridge, and pledges a grand reward to anyone able to pass his trial.","rew":"Experience: 160","done":"Hah! So you heard of my challenge, did you?\nWell sit down and listen. Have a drink, and savor it... because it might be your last.\nStormwind City Darnassus Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.6,"y":59.9,"n":"Wu Shen","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58.9,"y":35.3,"n":"Darnath Bladesinger","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":21.5,"y":44.7,"n":"Yorus Barleybrew","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5218":{"id":5218,"t":"Felstone Field Cauldron","lv":53,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Arcane Quickener sold by Alchemist Arbington , sold by Apothecary Dithers\n6 Osseous Agitator Skeletal Terror 50 % , Wandering Skeleton 50 % , Araj the Summoner 50 % , Skeletal Acolyte 50 % and 4 more\n4 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 525\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air. A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform.\nHaving already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.","done":"Adding the reagents to the cauldron's mix begins to change the color and texture of the cloud it spews forth. Scourge that are even remotely near the cauldron appear to recoil at the introduction of the new components into the environment.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":37.2,"y":56.8,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5058":{"id":5058,"t":"Mrs. Dalson's Diary","lv":55,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","done":"A diary with yellowing pages lies open to the last entry:\n\"I don't know what's going to happen now that Harold's turned. It took everything out of me to drag him into the only place I could find that'd lock him up tight and hold him. I hid the key on me, and I pray it works...\nI hope I can get out of here, but I need money to do that. Our stuff's all in the cabinet I think... and now that I think about it, doesn't Harold keep the key on him?\nI'll rest on it, I'm dead tired now.\"","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":47.8,"y":50.7,"n":"Mrs. Dalson's Diary","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5538":{"id":5538,"t":"Mold Rhymes With...","lv":57,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -15g instead of 0.","obj":"Bring the Imbued Skeletal Fragments and 15 gold coins to Krinkle Goodsteel in Gadgetzan.\nImbued Skeletal Fragments\nProvided: Imbued Skeletal Fragments","desc":"The goblin you will need to speak with is Krinkle Goodsteel. He peddles his skills to the highest bidder in Gadgetzan, within the Tanaris desert. He'll likely be the only one who can produce the mold we need, and his services won't come cheap. We now ask for you to dig deep by footing whatever fee he will charge.\nI'm an alchemist, not a banker. If I had gold lying around, I certainly wouldn't be here.\nI guess I said the quiet part out loud again. Oops.\nGadgetzan awaits you! Good luck!","rew":"Experience: 600","back":"Yeah, I know who you are, and I know why you're here. Arbington sent word to me before you arrived. Let's cut to deal at hand, now shall we?\nI've got a mold you can use for the skeleton key, but it will cost you - fifteen gold, up front, no negotiation. I'll pack the skeletal fragments into the mold for you, and I'll also teach you on how to forge the stem of the key without any knowledge of blacksmithing... all free of charge no less.\nWho says mercenaries don't offer competitive deals!","done":"Arbington said you'd deliver the goods, and deliver you have! A deal is a deal; let me pack the fragments into the mold for you.\nDid Arbington imbue them already? Excellent... otherwise, it would have been a long trip back to the Chillwind Point for you.\nWestern Plaguelands Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":83.8,"n":"Alchemist Arbington","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.5,"y":28.8,"n":"Krinkle Goodsteel","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"94898":{"id":94898,"t":"Violent winds temp disabled","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 10 Wind Hollows.\nWind Hollow slain : 0/ 10","desc":"When our home started to fall into the sky that fateful night, its as if the elements themselves were waiting to consume us. Wind spirits began appearing as we were fleeing, and to our dismay they began attacking the fleeing survivors.\nWe lost many villagers to the sky, but even more to the relentless anger of those wind spirits. I don't know if it was our village falling into the sky, but they are extremely dangerous.\nIf you are able, please put them to rest.\nZephras Isle Level 11 , requires level 8 Difficulty 8 9 14 17 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 94898","cats":["zephras-isle"]}});